  <event id="225">
      <start>11:45</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>AW1.120</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>The Cassandra distributed database</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>NoSQL</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://incubator.apache.org/cassandra/&#34;&gt;Apache Cassandra&lt;/a&gt; is a highly scalable second-generation distributed database, bringing together &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.allthingsdistributed.com/2007/10/amazons_dynamo.html&#34;&gt;Dynamo&lt;/a&gt;&amp;#39;s fully distributed design and &lt;a href=&#34;http://labs.google.com/papers/bigtable.html&#34;&gt;Bigtable&lt;/a&gt;&amp;#39;s ColumnFamily-based data model.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Cassandra is used at Facebook, Digg, Twitter, Mahalo, Ooyala, SimpleGEO, Rackspace, and other companies that need high scalability, availability, and fault tolerance.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will cover&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; Cassandra architecture and data model&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; Case studies: what people are using Cassandra for in production&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; Road map: where Cassandra development is headed&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2251">Eric Evans</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>